Overview:
We are looking for a Tech Lead Python to work with an international banking client. The role streamlines the integration of new data and technologies such as data virtualization and APIs, improving the accessibility and real-time availability of data across systems. You will work closely with Business Analysts, Solution Architects and other stakeholders, turning functional and technical requirements into scalable, high-quality applications and integrations.
What will you do?

• Design, develop and maintain solutions;

• Design, secure and scale back-end architectures;

• Design, develop and maintain APIs, microservices and event-driven integrations that support business processes and data exchanges;

• Implement solutions using APIs, data virtualization and related integration frameworks to improve data accessibility, consistency and real-time availability;

• Code and test the software components assigned to you within your technical domains;

• Industrialise the solution following CI/CD best practices;

• Contribute to the design, modelling and implementation of the product's solution, optimising code quality and future maintainability;

• Take part in the full software development lifecycle, including technical design, coding, unit testing, code reviews, defect resolution and deployment activities;

• Support Functional Testing and User Acceptance Testing (UAT) through defect analysis and resolution, ensuring solution quality and performance;

• Collaborate with Business Analysts, Solution Architects and other stakeholders to translate requirements into scalable solutions;

• Contribute to the functional and application consistency of the IT solution, ensuring service continuity and continuous development;

• Contribute to continuous improvement and innovation, delivering reliable and sustainable solutions aligned with business objectives.

What are we looking for?

• University Degree, or equivalent by experience, in Information Technology, Computer Science, Information Management or a related field;

• Mastery of Python development, including FastAPI, Flask and related frameworks;

• Strong experience in API design, RESTful services and microservices architectures;

• Experience with unit and integration testing using frameworks such as PyTest or Unittest;

• Experience with test management tools (e.g., ALM/Octane);

• Advanced SQL skills, including database design and optimisation (PostgreSQL preferred);

• Mastery of software engineering best practices, including CI/CD, Git workflows, code review, clean architecture, design patterns, unit testing and observability;

• Experience with cloud environments (AWS, IBM, etc.) and containerisation using Docker;

• Experience working in Agile/DevOps environments and with tools such as Jira, Confluence, Git and ALM;

• Ability to understand functional requests from end users, and to explain and support change;

• Good oral and written communication skills;

• Creativity, problem-solving skills and attention to detail;

• Strong teamwork and collaboration skills, and a good relationship between Business and IT;

• Experience in third-party data and data governance/management is a plus;

• Fluent in English;

• Notions of French.

What can you expect from us?

• A permanent job contract for a long term project;

• Tech equipment + SIM Card + personal smartphone;

• Health and Life Insurance;

• Social events and team buildings;

• The commitment of letting you grow with us, and be rewarded accordingly;

• A dynamic and young team that will be always there to support you;

• Training in the latest technologies;

• Coffee, fruits, snacks and a warm welcoming when you pass by the office.

